Ailang Native Browser — Full Implementation Plan

 Current State (Honest Assessment)

 What works: Block/inline text layout, basic flex, word wrapping, headings, paragraphs, color/font-size on direct
 elements, form element boxes (visual only), CSS rule matching (tag/class/id/combinators), HTTP GET with redirects
 and TLS (via openssl subprocess), DNS resolution with caching, cookie jar (basic), chunked transfer decoding, mouse
 wheel scrolling, link clicks, back/forward history, address bar navigation.

 What's broken/missing: CSS shorthand expansion (margin/padding/border shorthands silently ignored — this alone
 breaks 90% of sites), no CSS inheritance beyond color, no border rendering, no images, no inline-block, no position
 absolute/fixed, no float, no bold/italic fonts, only ~10 HTML entities, no event bubbling, fetch() is a stub, no
 POST method, no keyboard events in forms, no re-layout on DOM mutation, no requestAnimationFrame.

 Test262: 92.4% — the JS engine is solid. The browser shell around it is the problem.

 ---
 Tier 0: CSS Shorthand Expansion (Biggest Single Fix)

 Impact: Fixes spacing/layout on ~90% of all websites
 Effort: ~200 lines

 Almost every website uses margin: 10px 20px, padding: 8px, border: 1px solid #ccc. The CSS parser stores these as
 raw strings. The layout engine looks for margin-top, margin-left, etc. — which don't exist. Result: zero spacing
 everywhere.

 Tasks:

 1. Expand margin shorthand in CSSParse or at lookup time in HTMLLayout
   - margin: 10px → top/right/bottom/left = 10px
   - margin: 10px 20px → top/bottom=10px, right/left=20px
   - margin: 10px 20px 30px → top=10px, right/left=20px, bottom=30px
   - margin: 10px 20px 30px 40px → top=10, right=20, bottom=30, left=40
 2. Expand padding shorthand — same 1/2/3/4-value logic
 3. Expand border shorthand — border: 1px solid #ccc → border-width, border-style, border-color
 4. Expand background shorthand — at minimum extract background-color from background: #fff url(...)

 Files: Library.CSSParse.ailang (add CSS_ExpandShorthands function) or Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (expand at lookup
 time in LY__CSSLookupProp)

