 Tier 1: Core Visual Rendering

 Impact: Pages look like actual web pages instead of scattered text
 Effort: ~600-800 lines total

 1A. Border Rendering (~100 lines)

 Draw borders around elements. CSS properties already parsed.

 - Add LY__ResolveBorder in HTMLLayout — read border-width, border-style, border-color from CSS
 - Emit 4x FILL_RECT commands (top/right/bottom/left border edges) or a new DRAW_BORDER command
 - Account for border width in box model (reduce content area)
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang, Library.HTMLRender.ailang

 1B. CSS Property Inheritance (~150 lines)

 Make child elements inherit parent styles. Currently only color/font-size partially cascade.

 - Build inheritance stack: on block entry, push parent's computed
 color/font-size/font-family/text-align/line-height/font-weight
 - Children that don't have explicit CSS rules inherit from parent
 - On block exit, pop stack
 - Properties that inherit per CSS spec: color, font-size, font-family, font-weight, font-style, text-align,
 line-height, letter-spacing, word-spacing, white-space, visibility, cursor, list-style
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (add inheritance stack, modify LY__ResolveFgColor/LY__ResolveBgColor pattern for
 all inherited props)

 1C. Display: inline-block (~100 lines)

 Navigation bars, button groups, and grid-like patterns all use inline-block.

 - Track inline-block elements: they flow inline (same line as siblings) but have block dimensions (width/height)
 - Accumulate inline-block widths on current line, wrap when exceeding container width
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (add INLINE_BLOCK display type, modify inline flow logic)

 1D. Image Rendering (~200 lines)

 Fetch <img src>, decode, blit to canvas.

 - In browser_ipc.ailang: after DOM build, walk tree for <img> tags, fetch src via HTTP_Get
 - Decode: PNG/JPEG via external decoder subprocess (similar to gzip/openssl pattern) or BMP for simplicity
 - Store decoded pixels in per-image buffer
 - Layout: emit DRAW_IMAGE command with (x, y, w, h, pixel_ptr)
 - Render: implement Render__DrawImage — blit pixel buffer to canvas with clipping
 - Start with just width/height from attributes, no CSS sizing
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang, Library.HTMLRender.ailang, browser_ipc.ailang, new Library.ImageDecode.ailang
 (or subprocess approach)

 1E. Font Weight/Style (~50 lines, limited by TermFont)

 With only an 8x16 bitmap font, true bold/italic is impossible. But we can fake it:

 - Bold: draw character twice, offset 1px right (poor man's bold)
 - Italic: no good fake available, skip for now
 - Parse font-weight from CSS, store in layout state
 - Files: Library.HTMLRender.ailang (double-strike for bold), Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (resolve font-weight)

 1F. Text Decoration (~30 lines)

 Underline for links, strikethrough for <del>/<s>.

 - Underline: DRAW_LINE at baseline (y + font_h - 2) with text color
 - Strikethrough: DRAW_LINE at midpoint (y + font_h/2)
 - Parse text-decoration from CSS
 - Default: <a> gets underline
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (emit DRAW_LINE after DRAW_TEXT for decorated text)

