 Tier 3: Interactivity & Events

 Impact: Forms work, buttons respond, pages react to user input
 Effort: ~500-700 lines total

 3A. Event Bubbling (~100 lines)

 Currently events fire only on the target element. Real DOM events bubble up the tree.

 - JSBridge_FireEvent: after calling target's handlers, walk up DOM parent chain
 - At each ancestor: check for listeners on same event type, call them
 - Set event.target = original target, event.currentTarget = current node
 - Honor stopPropagation() — break the walk
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang (modify FireEvent loop)

 3B. Keyboard Events (~100 lines)

 Forms need keyboard input. Currently no keydown/keyup/keypress events.

 - browser_ipc.ailang already receives key events from display server
 - Map key codes to DOM KeyboardEvent properties (key, code, keyCode, which)
 - Fire keydown, keypress, keyup on focused element
 - Update <input> value on printable key press
 - Handle backspace, enter, tab, escape
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang (key event dispatch), Library.JSBridge.ailang (KeyboardEvent object creation)

 3C. Focus/Blur Events (~50 lines)

 - Track focused element in BrState
 - Fire focus on element when clicked/tabbed to
 - Fire blur on previous element
 - Update :focus pseudo-class state (for CSS, future)
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang, Library.JSBridge.ailang

 3D. Input/Change Events (~50 lines)

 - Fire input event on every keystroke in <input>/<textarea>
 - Fire change event on blur if value changed
 - Sync DOM attribute "value" with JS property
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang, browser_ipc.ailang

 3E. Form Submission via POST (~100 lines)

 - Detect <form method="POST">
 - Collect all input values (name=value pairs)
 - URL-encode body: name1=val1&name2=val2
 - Send via HTTP POST (need to add HTTP_Post to HTTPClient)
 - Content-Type: application/x-www-form-urlencoded
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang, Library.HTTPClient.ailang (add HTTP__DoPost)

 3F. DOMContentLoaded / load Events (~50 lines)

 - Fire DOMContentLoaded on document after DOM build + inline script execution
 - Fire load on window after all resources (CSS, images, scripts) loaded
 - Many sites gate initialization on these events
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang (fire events at appropriate pipeline stages), Library.JSBridge.ailang

 3G. requestAnimationFrame (~50 lines)

 - Currently stubbed (no-op). Many sites use rAF for animations and rendering.
 - Store callback in pool, fire all pending callbacks once per frame tick (~60fps)
 - Browser event loop calls JSBridge_TickRAF(timestamp) each frame
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang (implement rAF pool + tick), browser_ipc.ailang (call tick from event loop)

