 Tier 4: Networking & Resources

 Impact: External resources load, AJAX works, sessions persist
 Effort: ~400-500 lines total

 4A. Real fetch() API (~150 lines)

 Replace the stub with actual HTTP requests.

 - Parse URL from fetch() argument
 - Make HTTP_Get (or HTTP_Post) call via HTTPClient
 - Build Response object with real status, statusText, headers
 - response.text() → return body as string
 - response.json() → parse body via JSON library
 - Handle errors (network failure → rejected Promise)
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang (handlers 140-142), Library.HTTPClient.ailang

 4B. External Script Loading (Re-enable) (~50 lines)

 The 3-step API already exists. Re-enable with per-script timeout.

 - Set a 5-second timeout per script fetch (not 180s)
 - Skip scripts that fail to fetch (don't block layout)
 - Log fetch results for debugging
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang (re-enable step 2 with timeout)

 4C. Content-Encoding: gzip (~50 lines)

 Many servers send gzip by default. The browser sends Accept-Encoding: gzip.

 - After HTTP response, check Content-Encoding header
 - If gzip: pipe body through gzip -d subprocess (pattern already exists in HTTPGzip.ailang)
 - Replace body with decompressed content
 - Files: Library.HTTPClient.ailang or Library.HTTPGzip.ailang (verify/fix existing implementation)

 4D. Cookie Jar Fixes (~50 lines)

 - Honor path matching (only send cookies for matching path prefix)
 - Parse Max-Age/Expires (session vs persistent)
 - Honor Secure flag (only send on HTTPS)
 - Files: Library.HTTPCookie.ailang

 4E. localStorage (~50 lines)

 Replace stubs with file-backed persistence.

 - Store at ~/.ailang_browser/localStorage/<origin>.json
 - getItem/setItem/removeItem read/write JSON file
 - 5MB limit per origin (spec)
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang (handlers 127-129)

