 Tier 5: CSS Advanced Features

 Impact: Modern sites render correctly
 Effort: ~600 lines total

 5A. rgb()/rgba() Color Parsing (~80 lines)

 Many sites use rgb(255, 0, 0) or rgba(0,0,0,0.5) instead of hex.

 - Parse rgb(r, g, b) and rgba(r, g, b, a) in LY__ParseColor
 - Handle percentages: rgb(100%, 0%, 50%)
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (extend LY__ParseColor)

 5B. CSS calc() (~100 lines)

 - Parse calc(100% - 20px) expressions
 - Support: +, -, *, / operators with px, %, em, vw, vh units
 - Evaluate at layout time when container width is known
 - Files: Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (extend LY__ParsePx)

 5C. Media Queries (~100 lines)

 - Parse @media (max-width: 768px) { ... }
 - Evaluate against current viewport dimensions
 - Include/exclude rules based on match
 - Support: min-width, max-width, min-height, max-height
 - Files: Library.CSSParse.ailang (parse @media), Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (evaluate conditions)

 5D. CSS Variables (~100 lines)

 - Parse --custom-prop: value declarations
 - Resolve var(--custom-prop) at property lookup time
 - Inheritance: variables cascade like other inherited properties
 - Files: Library.CSSParse.ailang, Library.HTMLLayout.ailang

 5E. Pseudo-selectors: :hover, :focus (~80 lines)

 - Track hovered element (mouse position → hit test each frame)
 - Track focused element (click/tab)
 - Re-evaluate CSS rules when hover/focus state changes
 - Trigger re-layout + re-render on state change
 - Files: Library.CSSParse.ailang (store pseudo-selector type), Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (match against element
 state), browser_ipc.ailang (track hover/focus state)

 5F. Named HTML Entities (~100 lines, mostly data)

 Only ~10 entities work. HTML5 has 2,127. Add the common ~200:

 - &mdash; (8212), &ndash; (8211), &rsquo; (8217), &lsquo; (8216)
 - &ldquo; (8220), &rdquo; (8221), &bull; (8226), &hellip; (8230)
 - &trade; (8482), &reg; (174), &euro; (8364), &pound; (163)
 - Build lookup table: hash entity name → codepoint
 - Files: Library.HTMLTokenizer.ailang (extend HTK__DecodeEntity)

