 Tier 6: DOM Mutation Re-render

 Impact: Dynamic pages update visually after JS changes the DOM
 Effort: ~200 lines

 6A. Dirty Flag + Re-layout (~100 lines)

 - Set BrState.dirty = 1 when DOM is mutated (appendChild, removeChild, innerHTML set, style change)
 - In event loop: if dirty, re-run Layout_Run + Render_Exec + ShmCanvas_Present
 - Batch mutations: don't re-layout on every single DOM change, wait for next frame tick
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang (dirty check in event loop), Library.JSBridge.ailang (set dirty flag on mutations)

 6B. getComputedStyle (~100 lines)

 - Replace stub with real implementation
 - After layout, read computed values from layout state for a given DOM node
 - Return object with all CSS properties and their computed values
 - Files: Library.JSBridge.ailang (handler 123), Library.HTMLLayout.ailang (store per-node computed values)

 ---
 Tier 7: Performance & Polish

 Impact: Browser feels responsive, pages load fast
 Effort: ~300 lines

 7A. HTTP Keep-Alive / Connection Pooling (~150 lines)

 Every HTTPS request forks an openssl process (~200ms). Loading a page with 10 CSS + 30 JS files = 8+ seconds just on
  TLS handshakes.

 - Keep openssl subprocess alive for same host
 - Reuse pipe for multiple requests (HTTP/1.1 keep-alive)
 - Pool up to 4 connections per host
 - Files: Library.HTTPClient.ailang (major refactor of DoGetTLS)

 7B. Keyboard Scrolling (~30 lines)

 - Page Up/Down: scroll by viewport height
 - Home/End: scroll to top/bottom
 - Arrow Up/Down: scroll by 48px
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang (key handler)

 7C. Parallel Resource Loading (~100 lines)

 Currently CSS and JS files are fetched sequentially. Fork multiple curl/openssl processes and poll them.

 - Use non-blocking I/O + poll() to wait on multiple subprocesses
 - Fetch up to 4 resources simultaneously
 - Files: browser_ipc.ailang, Library.HTTPClient.ailang (async fetch API)

