 ---
 Recommended Priority for "Make It Usable"

 If you want to see the fastest visual improvement and reach "usable basic browser":

 1. Tier 0 — CSS shorthand expansion (instant improvement on every site)
 2. Tier 1B — CSS inheritance (text colors/sizes cascade properly)
 3. Tier 1A — Border rendering (visual structure appears)
 4. Tier 1C — inline-block (navigation bars work)
 5. Tier 3B — Keyboard events (can type in forms)
 6. Tier 3E — POST method (search forms work)
 7. Tier 1D — Image rendering (pages look real)
 8. Tier 2A — Float (classic multi-column layouts)
 9. Tier 2B — Position absolute/fixed (modals, dropdowns)
 10. Tier 4A — Real fetch() (AJAX-driven pages work)

 After items 1-6, you'd have a browser that can render most static sites correctly and submit search forms. After all
  10, you'd cover the majority of non-SPA websites.

